## When to open a PR (locked)

Global rule: `~/.cursor/rules/github-pr-draft-until-ready.mdc` (all repos).

- **Do not** open a review PR on the first commit while overnight/multi-tick work is still landing more commits on the same concern.
- Finish the commits you want in that PR (or a coherent first slice you are ready to land alone), push the branch, **then** open the PR.
- Prefer **`--draft`** until the branch is ready for review:

```bash
gh pr create --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --base dev --head Interchouette:<feat> --draft
# when ready:
gh pr ready <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs
gh pr edit <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --add-reviewer gRoussac
```

- Request **`--reviewer gRoussac` only when marking ready** (or on create if the PR is complete and not draft).
- Extra follow-up commits on an already-ready PR are for review fixes only, not “still building the feature.”

## Merge style (fork rebase + squash)

| Step | Who / where | Action |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Keep PR current | **Fork** | `git fetch interchouette && git rebase interchouette/dev` on the feature branch, then push to `interchouette` (SSH-signed). |
| Reviewer | Ready PRs | Always `--reviewer gRoussac` (not while still draft-building). |
| Merge gate | **gRoussac Approve** | Comments = babysit only. Never merge without Approve. |
| Org enforcement | Branch protection on `dev` | **1** approving review + **code owner** review; admins included; no force pushes. |
| Land on org | After Approve | `gh pr merge --squash` with conventional PR title as the squash subject. |
| Forbidden default | Agent | `gh pr merge --rebase` onto org (GitHub rewrites commits and drops Verified). |
| Forbidden | Agent | `gh pr merge` when `reviews` has no `APPROVED` from **gRoussac** (chat “merge anyway” does not count). |

```bash
# Ready (non-draft) create:
gh pr create --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --base dev --head Interchouette:<feat> --reviewer gRoussac
# or promote draft:
gh pr ready <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs
gh pr edit <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --add-reviewer gRoussac
```

CODEOWNERS: `* @gRoussac` in repo-root `CODEOWNERS`. Creds: `.github_credentials`. Actions: `.github/workflows/`.

## Workflow (every change)

```text
fork: create feat/… from interchouette/dev
 → signed conventional commits + push interchouette feat/… (finish the concern first)
 → rebase onto interchouette/dev on the fork if behind (signed)
 → gh pr create … --draft   (or create ready only if the slice is complete)
 → when ready: gh pr ready + --reviewer gRoussac
 → confirm PR head Verified
 → wait gRoussac Approve, then --squash
 → sync fork: git fetch upstream && git checkout dev && git merge --ff-only upstream/dev && git push interchouette dev
 → prune local (delete the feature branch on the fork and locally)
```

### After merge (locked)

A **MERGED** or **CLOSED** PR is dead. Further work does **not** go on that PR or its head branch.

1. Before any push you would describe as “to PR #N”, run `gh pr view <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --json state,mergedAt`.
2. If `state` is `MERGED` or `CLOSED`: **stop**. Do **not** `git push` that head branch and claim it updates the PR. Org `dev` will not move.
3. Leftover commits: new branch from `upstream/dev` (or synced `interchouette/dev`), new PR. Never revive a merged PR by pushing the old head.
4. After squash-merge: sync fork `dev`, then **delete** the feature branch on the fork (`git push interchouette --delete <branch>`) and locally. A surviving fork branch after merge is garbage, not an open PR.

Pushing more commits onto a merged PR’s head (or a deleted/recreated leftover of it) is forbidden agent failure. It does not land on the org.

1. Prefer **create under Interchouette-ITC**, then **fork to Interchouette**.
2. Day-to-day remote **`interchouette`** = fork; **`upstream`** = org. Do **not** name the worker remote `origin`.
3. **Never** `git push upstream`. Org code lands **only** by PR merge.
4. On the **fork**, commit and push freely to `interchouette` (only while the PR for that branch is still **OPEN**).

## Bootstrap

Done: org [`Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs`](https://github.com/Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs), fork [`Interchouette/tvscreener-rs`](https://github.com/Interchouette/tvscreener-rs), remotes `upstream` + `interchouette`, default branch `dev`.

Day-to-day work uses the workflow above. Do **not** invent a second integration branch.

## Do not

- Merge without **gRoussac** Approve (verify via `gh pr view … --json reviews` first).
- Lower or bypass org branch protection (`required_approving_review_count`, code owners, `enforce_admins`).
- Open a **ready** PR before the commits for that concern are done (use **draft**, or wait).
- Open a PR without requesting **gRoussac** once it is ready for review.
- Rely on Cursor chat alone for Approve (use GitHub review + `--reviewer gRoussac`).
- Push to a **merged or closed** PR head, or keep using a feature branch after merge as if the PR were still open.
- Say “pushed to #N” without checking that #N is still `OPEN`.
- Force-push to `dev` on org or fork (protection forbids force pushes on org `dev`).
